      <Comment source="xue, PMN, nilo-poyanco">|FRAME: KDO| (known as Kdo for ketodeoxyoctonate) is a part of the inner core of lipopolysaccharides. It is added to the lipid A precursor |FRAME: LIPID-IV-A| in sequential steps, with different Kdo units added by different linkages. The first unit is always added by a (2-&gt;6) glycosidic linkage and the second one by a (2-&gt;4) linkage. The actual donor of Kdo units is its activated form, CMP-Kdo.</Comment>
